{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1509295-bane-arrows","id":1509295,"title":"Bane Arrows","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-22T09:56:51-07:00","id":1509295,"title":"Bane Arrows","content":"I have a stupid question, but how do you guys use Bane Arrows?<br /> <br /> &quot;They hit Automatically and do 3 dice of Aggravated Damage.&quot;<br /> <br /> So when you use your Archery roll to shoot a bane, they hit automatically, but do they /only/ do 3 dice of agg damage? Does that mean they take an automatic 3 HL's/Power Points of damage, or do you have to roll the 3 dice? Do you add your archery successes into the damage pool, or is it only 3 dice/damage? <br /> <br /> I feel like it should be better explained, or at the least, they feel underpowered.<br /> <br /> Any thoughts?\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23998-dynamiterave","name":"DynamiteRave","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T11:09:18-07:00","id":1509303,"title":"","content":"The main power of the Bane Arrows is that they automatically hit Banes even if they are unseen (and howl afterwards). The original description in the 1e corebook does not mention the three aggravated damage, it just says they inflict damage as usual. That got added in later editions.<br /> <br /> So I would say 1) you need to roll the damage dice (it is not automatic damage) and 2) if your rules set say you can transform archery successes into additional damage, then you can add those to your damage pool as well (meaning they too are aggravated). If the Archery roll gets no successes or botches, then just roll the three dice (it hits anyway, so ignore any failure or botches).<br /> <br /> Since a spirit's &quot;health levels&quot; are their Essence (or Power Level in earlier editions), I'm not sure why it's important it does aggravated damage to them. All damage types equally reduce the relevant spirit's trait. It would only really have an impact if the spirit was Materialized and had Health Levels.<br /> <br /> I don't think the idea of the Bane Arrow is to kill the Bane. So if that is what you are hoping for, it will always be underpowered. It is that it unerringly hits it (even if unseen) and causes it to howl, so it alerts all Garou in an area that there is a Bane nearby. Then the Garou all dogpile it.<br /> <br /> I think the real question is whether the Bane Arrow was meant to be launched in the physical world and yet still hit a Bane that is in the Penumbra, or if it was a Talen that could only hit things on the plane the Garou was in. In early Werewolf, not everything was very clear and later editions typically did not clarify things. But I think the case can be made that it was originally tended for Garou to be able to shoot the arrow while in the physical realm, yet hit a Bane in the Penumbra so they can hear it howling. Charms that make a spirit unseen or invisible are very rare - they aren't typical. So I think the idea of a Bane not being visible indicates the Bane would be on the other side of the Gauntlet. Obviously the description of the Talen does not adequately describe the mechanics if this was so. But as I said, there is a lot unclarity in the early sourcebooks, and later corebooks would often just reprint whole sections verbatim or with minor changes, instead of incorporating necessary rules in subsequent sourcebooks or clarify things on their own in the new edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}